{"plan":{"about":"The work-in-progress schedule testing the F1 Finance Audit Machine follows for the invented HANGS General Contracting LP at its June 30, 2026 year end. The runner reads its rates and thresholds from here; the Job Files system shows it. Every name and figure is invented.","engagement":"FY2026 Work-in-Progress Schedule Testing","entity":"HANGS General Contracting LP","period":"The job schedule at June 30, 2026, the end of fiscal 2026","reader":"The owners, the bonding company and the lender read the year-end statements; the bonding company reads the job schedule closely.","materiality":{"benchmark":"Contract revenue for the year","rate":"0.005","roundDownTo":10000,"performance":"0.75","trivial":"0.05","why":"A contractor's income swings with its job estimates, so revenue is the steadier benchmark. The same materiality serves every FY2026 audit area of HGC. The engagement partner sets the final amounts."},"retainage":"0.05","fade":{"points":"0.01","rule":"A job's margin is investigated when it moved more than one percentage point from its bid or from the prior year end, and every job is checked for an expected loss at June 30 and after the costs that came later."},"procedures":[{"stage":"Plan the Job Testing","what":"Agree the trial balance, propose materiality from the year's revenue, and rebuild the year's revenue and costs from the schedules of active and completed jobs."},{"stage":"Recompute the Jobs","what":"Recompute percent complete and earned revenue on every job at June 30, 2026 and at the prior year end, and tie the over and under billings to the balance sheet."},{"stage":"Vouch the Change Orders","what":"Agree each contract to its original amount and change orders, and vouch every change order to the owner's signed approval: the amount and the date."},{"stage":"Test the Estimates","what":"Set each job's estimated cost to complete at June 30 against the costs it actually ran in July to September and its September 30 estimate, and read why an